# Soul and Juice

This game is deliberately juiced. Do not add mechanics that only mutate state.
Reasoning behind each rule is in `docs/SOUL.md`.

## Feel constants are centralised

Every duration, amplitude, and curve lives in `src/utils/juice.ts` as a named
constant. Never inline a feel number in a component.

```tsx
// BAD - a magic number nobody can tune
setTimeout(() => setDyingPieces([]), 260);

// GOOD
setTimeout(() => setDyingPieces([]), JUICE.deathMs);
```

## Every player action answers in at least two senses

A new action needs sound plus something visual (motion, colour, or shake).
`soundEngine` is pure synthesis, so add a method there rather than an audio file.
Repeated sounds must go through `vary()` / `varyGain()` so the tenth move does
not sound identical to the first.

## Consequences persist

Captures append to `scars` and survive reload via the `hnefatafl_save` blob.
Only `handleNewGame` clears them. If you add a destructive event, leave a mark.

## Motion is opt-out

Gate anything kinetic on `settings.juiceEnabled`, and use `useScreenShake` or
`useReducedMotion` so `prefers-reduced-motion` is respected structurally.

## Role colours live in ROLE_META

Add a field to `ROLE_META` in `src/utils/roles.ts`. Never hardcode amber or sky
into a component.

## Compatibility surfaces

`Move.captures` stays `Position[]` and new `Move` fields stay optional. That type
crosses the socket in `MovePayload` and sits in saved games, so widening it
breaks online play against un-updated clients and existing saves.

## Narrative must read the board

`sagaVoice.ts` picks lines from what actually happened: who fell, where the piece
landed, whether the king's road opened. Never add a random flavour-text pool that
ignores position.
